  "theoryOfChange": "World Central Kitchen is a frontline force that shows up with the urgency of now where others can\u2019t or won\u2019t. Key goals of WCK\u2019s work are to:1) Deliver warm, fresh meals to communities without food access due to acute crises. WCK\u2019s relief model delivers warm meals and other food support directly to communities while boosting livelihoods, businesses, and economies. WCK has served hundreds of millions of meals through comforting plates of food, kits full of fresh ingredients, and produce boxes, supporting communities affected by hurricanes, floods, humanitarian crises, conflict, and other disasters.2) Work side by side with local vendors, volunteers, restaurants, and community organizations to invest resources back into crisis-afflicted areas. WCK\u2019s Response Corps members\u2014trained local chefs and contractors\u2014often join relief efforts and introduce WCK to community organizations and restaurants in the area. The support of Response Corps, Chef Corps (a global network of hundreds of culinary leaders who champion WCK\u2019s work), and other local partners enable them to serve meals immediately. WCK also works with local food suppliers, hires from within the community, and collaborates with NGOs.3) Provide comfort, hope, and love through their food service. A warm meal\u2014tailored to the culture and recipes of the local community\u2014can bring more than nutrition and calories. WCK utilizes the unique power of food to provide hope, comfort, and the reassurance that communities are not alone during times of crises. During the response to the severe flooding in the Valencia region of Spain brought upon by storm DANA in October 2024, WCK supported the residents of hard-hit Paiporte. A resident shared, \u201cWe haven\u2019t eaten a hot plate of food in days; many of the neighbors do not have power at home or gas and we cannot even heat a plate of food. Thank you for giving us hot meals; we really needed it.\u201d",
